WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.838
Retrieval is the decision layer that chooses what evidence reaches the model.

2
00:00:04.838 --> 00:00:09.969
A RAG system usually cannot send the entire knowledge base into the context window.

3
00:00:09.969 --> 00:00:20.012
It selects a limited set of chunks using query processing, filters, similarity search, keyword matching, ranking, reranking, source rules, and context limits.

4
00:00:20.012 --> 00:00:23.971
Those decisions strongly influence answer quality and safety.

5
00:00:23.971 --> 00:00:32.547
Retrieval should be constrained by user permissions, tenant scope, workflow purpose, source eligibility, and freshness requirements.

6
00:00:32.547 --> 00:00:41.637
A user should not receive a chunk just because it is semantically similar when the source is restricted, expired, or outside the approved workflow.

7
00:00:41.637 --> 00:00:44.203
More retrieved text is not always better.

8
00:00:44.203 --> 00:00:53.146
Too much context can crowd out important evidence, introduce stale or conflicting material, increase cost, and make the answer harder to steer.

9
00:00:53.146 --> 00:01:04.801
Retrieval design should consider top-k choices, relevance thresholds, duplicate handling, source diversity, freshness preferences, and no-answer behavior when the evidence is weak.

10
00:01:04.801 --> 00:01:08.100
Context assembly is also an architectural boundary.

11
00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:15.870
The final prompt should separate trusted system instructions, application policy, user requests, and retrieved evidence.

12
00:01:15.870 --> 00:01:21.588
Retrieved chunks should be labeled as source material rather than treated as system policy.

13
00:01:21.588 --> 00:01:27.526
That separation helps the model use evidence without confusing it with higher-priority rules.

14
00:01:27.526 --> 00:01:31.778
A mature private RAG system makes retrieval observable and tunable.

15
00:01:31.778 --> 00:01:43.433
Engineers should be able to see which chunks were considered, which filters were applied, why certain sources were selected, and whether the answer was grounded in the retrieved material.

16
00:01:43.433 --> 00:01:47.392
Retrieval settings should be reviewed as requirements change.

17
00:01:47.392 --> 00:01:59.047
A workflow that supports exploratory research may need different ranking, source diversity, and no-answer behavior than a workflow used for policy guidance or customer-facing support.
